## Code availability
The Gaussian code, used to perform the ab initio cluster calculations, can be licensed from Gaussian, Inc. (see https://gaussian.com/). The QuickFF (used to derive the force fields), Yaff (MD engine) and ThermoLIB (free energy evaluation engine) software packages are freely accessible via https://molmod.ugent.be/software/. The MEPSA code for the minimal free energy path analysis is freely available at http://bioweb.cbm.uam.es/ software/MEPSA/. Representative input and processing scripts are available at https:// github.com/SanderBorgmans/SupportingInformation.
